---
pagination:
  data: redirects
  size: 1
  alias: redirect
permalink: "{{ redirect.from }}index.html"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- One page per old WordPress address. It has no layout of its own: nothing
    here should look like part of the site, because nobody is meant to stay
    long enough to read it. The meta refresh moves the reader, the canonical
    tag tells search engines which address counts, noindex keeps the page
    itself out of results, and the link in the body is there for anyone whose
    browser ignores the refresh. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ redirect.to }}">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://amirkhesro.com{{ redirect.to }}">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <title>Page moved</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>This page has moved to <a href="{{ redirect.to }}">https://amirkhesro.com{{ redirect.to }}</a>.</p>
  </body>
</html>
